cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the corpus, please cite it as below."
title: "flux-kegonsa: an LES-trained flux-footprint emulator for the Kegonsa Solar Array eddy-covariance tower"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tyagi
    given-names: Atharva
repository-code: "https://github.com/tyatharva/flux-kegonsa"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
keywords:
  - flux footprint
  - eddy covariance
  - large-eddy simulation
  - Lagrangian particle dispersion
  - Fourier neural operator
  - flow matching
  - FastEddy
abstract: >-
  A site-calibrated emulator that predicts two-dimensional flux footprints for one
  eddy-covariance tower from the six scalar inputs of the Kljun et al. (2015)
  parameterisation. Training targets come from 1366 large-eddy simulations (FastEddy)
  with a backward Lagrangian particle model; the emulator is a Fourier neural operator
  predicting a residual on Kljun, with a flow-matching variant for sample spread.
